## How to Use

### Step 1: Open the Application
Navigate to: [C:\Users\samsung\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\solar-pv-calculator\index.html](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/index.html)

### Step 2: Enter Parameters
Fill in your solar PV system details:
- Project information (name, location, coordinates)
- System configuration (power, losses, orientation)
- Climate and performance settings

### Step 3: Calculate
Click the **"Calculate System Performance"** button to generate the analysis

### Step 4: Review Results
The application will display:
- Comprehensive summary of your inputs
- Monthly performance data table
- Interactive charts and visualizations
- Annual statistics

### Step 5: Export (Optional)
Click **"Export PDF"** to download a professional report

## Technical Implementation

### Files Created

- [index.html](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/index.html) - Main application structure (323 lines)
- [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/styles.css) - Premium design system (467 lines)
- [app.js](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/app.js) - Calculation engine (563 lines)

### Technologies Used

- **HTML5** - Semantic structure
- **CSS3** - Modern styling with custom properties, gradients, glassmorphism
- **JavaScript (ES6+)** - Object-oriented calculator class
- **Chart.js** - Professional data visualizations
- **jsPDF** - PDF generation
- **html2canvas** - Report rendering
- **Google Fonts (Inter)** - Premium typography

### Calculation Models

The application uses scientifically-based solar models:

**Irradiation Calculation:**
```javascript
irradiation = baseRadiation × seasonalFactor × latitudeFactor × tiltFactor × azimuthFactor
```

**Energy Production:**
```javascript
energy = pvPower × irradiation × systemEfficiency × days
```

**Performance Ratio:**
```javascript
PR = basePR - temperatureLosses - additionalLosses
```

